Well, you should set R_HOME in the first place ;).
On unix (which includes Macs) it is quite easy, because you can use  
"R CMD" to setup everything you need, e.g.
R CMD java -jar myApp.jar

As of the JRI library, it has to be on the java.library.path, so you  
either set it to point to your path or you put JRI in the start  
directory - whichever is more convenient for you,.

Cheers,
Simon


